{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  OTODOR Module: Offer Popup  (seasonal campaign / coupon)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose:            Put the running campaign in front of a visitor once —
                      the coupon, what it applies to, what the price becomes,
                      and a one-tap copy of the code.
  Primary source:     Theme settings → OTODOR Offers, Pricing & EMI (campaign
                      name, coupon code, value, scope, delivery, GST, EMI), so
                      the popup, the promo strip and every product offer panel
                      quote the same offer.
  Fallback order:     Section overrides (heading / body / code / CTA) → theme
                      settings → hide the line.
  Visibility rule:    Renders nothing unless the offer layer is on AND the
                      campaign window is open AND there is a coupon code AND
                      the current page is in the chosen targeting. The visitor
                      then sees it at most once per "show again" period, and
                      never again after they copy the code.
  Merchant editable:  YES — copy, image, trigger timing, targeting, frequency.
  Required metafields: none.
  Optional metafields: none.
  Dependencies:       otodor-campaign-live, otodor-rupees, otodor-icon;
                      assets/otodor-offer.js (dialog behaviour + copy button);
                      otodor-base.css tokens.
  Placement:          Rendered once sitewide from layout/theme.liquid, so one
                      configuration covers every page. Targeting decides where
                      it actually appears.
  Accessibility:      role="dialog" aria-modal, labelled by its heading, focus
                      moved in and restored on close, ESC closes, focus trapped
                      while open, backdrop click closes, reduced motion honoured.

  A POPUP THAT CANNOT BE DISMISSED FOR GOOD IS A TAX ON RETURNING CUSTOMERS.
  Dismissal is remembered for `remember_days`; copying the code suppresses it
  for a year. Both are localStorage, keyed by the coupon code — change the
  campaign and everyone sees the new one.
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Captures sit outside the {% liquid %} block: that tag reads one line per tag,
  so a multi-line `render` inside it would be truncated. Same idiom as the
  product modules.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture campaign_live -%}
  {%- render 'otodor-campaign-live' -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture product_scope -%}
  {%- render 'otodor-module-applies',
    module_id: 'coupon',
    product: product,
    only_collections: settings.otodor_coupon_collections,
    only_tags: settings.otodor_coupon_tags -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- liquid
  assign campaign_live = campaign_live | strip
  assign product_scope = product_scope | strip

  assign coupon_code = section.settings.code_override | default: settings.otodor_coupon_code
  assign coupon_amount = settings.otodor_coupon_amount | plus: 0

  # ── Targeting: which pages may show it ───────────────────────────────
  assign target = section.settings.target | default: 'all'
  assign in_target = false
  case target
    when 'all'
      assign in_target = true
    when 'home'
      if request.page_type == 'index'
        assign in_target = true
      endif
    when 'shopping'
      if request.page_type == 'index' or request.page_type == 'collection' or request.page_type == 'product' or request.page_type == 'list-collections'
        assign in_target = true
      endif
    when 'scoped'
      # Only where the coupon can actually be used.
      if request.page_type == 'collection' and collection != blank
        assign scope_handles = settings.otodor_coupon_collections | split: ','
        for handle in scope_handles
          assign wanted = handle | strip | downcase
          if wanted != blank and collection.handle == wanted
            assign in_target = true
            break
          endif
        endfor
      elsif request.page_type == 'product' and product != blank
        if product_scope == 'true'
          assign in_target = true
        endif
      endif
  endcase

  assign show_popup = false
  if section.settings.enabled and campaign_live == '1' and coupon_code != blank and in_target
    assign show_popup = true
  endif

  assign popup_key = coupon_code | handle
-%}

{%- if show_popup -%}
  {%- style -%}
    .otodor-pop {
      position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 100;
      display: none; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      padding: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    }
    .otodor-pop[data-open="true"] { display: flex; }
    {%- comment -%}
      No `both` fill on either entry animation. With it, the first keyframe
      (opacity 0) is held whenever the animation has not started — and an
      animation does not advance while the document timeline is stalled: a
      background tab, a throttled renderer, a headless/non-compositing
      browser. The modal is then laid out, focused and hit-testable while
      being completely invisible, which is indistinguishable from "the popup
      is broken".

      Without the fill, the resting state is the visible one and the
      animation is pure decoration: if it never runs, the popup simply
      appears without its fade. Visibility must never depend on motion.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    .otodor-pop__backdrop {
      position: absolute; inset: 0;
      background: rgba(6, 6, 6, 0.74);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(3px); backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
      animation: otodor-pop-fade 220ms ease;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      Sized like a store's offer modal, not a landing page: one column of
      content at a readable measure, the image as a supporting panel. The
      scale below is deliberately a step down from the page's display type —
      a modal that shouts reads as an ad, not as an offer.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    .otodor-pop__dialog {
      position: relative;
      width: min({% if section.settings.image != blank %}59rem{% else %}34rem{% endif %}, 100%);
      max-height: calc(100vh - 2rem);
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: {% if section.settings.image != blank %}0.78fr 1fr{% else %}1fr{% endif %};
      overflow: hidden;
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: #101010;
      color: var(--otodor-white, #fff);
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      box-shadow: 0 24px 70px rgba(0,0,0,0.55);
      animation: otodor-pop-rise 300ms cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
    }
    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      .otodor-pop__dialog { grid-template-columns: 1fr; width: min(30rem, 100%); }
      .otodor-pop__media { display: none; }
    }
    .otodor-pop__media { position: relative; overflow: hidden; background: #0B0B0B; }
    .otodor-pop__media img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }

    .otodor-pop__body {
      padding: clamp(1.8rem, 2.6vw, 2.4rem);
      display: grid; gap: 0; align-content: center;
      overflow-y: auto;
    }

    .otodor-pop__eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: 0.86rem; font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5);
    }
    .otodor-pop__title {
      font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 2.6vw, 2.15rem);
      font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.14; letter-spacing: var(--otodor-tracking-tight, -0.02em);
      margin: 0.7rem 0 0; color: var(--otodor-white, #fff);
    }
    .otodor-pop__text {
      margin: 0.6rem 0 0; font-size: 1.12rem; line-height: 1.6;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.58); max-width: 30rem;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      The coupon reads as one control: code on the left, a single copy
      action on the right, divided by a hairline. Nothing about it is
      decorative — a visitor's whole job here is to take the code away.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    .otodor-pop__coupon {
      display: flex; align-items: stretch; margin-top: 1.6rem;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16);
      border-radius: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .otodor-pop__code {
      flex: 1 1 auto; display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
      padding: 0.85rem 1rem; min-width: 0;
      font-family: var(--otodor-font-body); font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--otodor-white, #fff);
      overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .otodor-pop__copy {
      flex: 0 0 auto; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      cursor: pointer; padding: 0 1.35rem; border: none;
      /* Holds its width when the label swaps to "Copied", so the coupon
         field doesn't jump under the visitor's cursor. */
      min-width: 7rem;
      border-left: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.16);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04); color: var(--otodor-blue, #4DA6FF);
      font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase;
      transition: background 160ms ease, color 160ms ease;
    }
    .otodor-pop__copy:hover { background: rgba(77,166,255,0.12); }
    .otodor-pop__copy[data-copied="true"] { color: #25D366; background: rgba(37,211,102,0.12); }

    .otodor-pop__value {
      margin: 0.7rem 0 0; font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.5;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);
    }
    .otodor-pop__value strong { color: var(--otodor-white, #fff); font-weight: 600; }

    .otodor-pop__perks {
      list-style: none; margin: 1.3rem 0 0; padding: 1.1rem 0 0;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.45rem 1.4rem;
    }
    .otodor-pop__perk {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem;
      font-size: 0.98rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);
    }
    .otodor-pop__perk svg { width: 13px; height: 13px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.35); }

    .otodor-pop__actions { display: grid; gap: 0.55rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
    .otodor-pop__cta {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.5rem;
      min-height: 46px; padding: 0.75rem 1.4rem;
      border-radius: var(--otodor-radius-pill, 999px);
      background: var(--otodor-white, #fff); color: #0B0B0B;
      font-family: var(--otodor-font-display); font-size: 1.14rem; font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none; transition: background 160ms ease;
    }
    .otodor-pop__cta:hover { background: #E8E8E8; }
    .otodor-pop__cta svg { width: 14px; height: 14px; }
    .otodor-pop__later {
      background: none; border: none; cursor: pointer; padding: 0.5rem;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); font-family: inherit; font-size: 1rem;
      transition: color 160ms ease;
    }
    .otodor-pop__later:hover { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); }
    .otodor-pop__fine {
      margin: 1.1rem 0 0; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.3);
    }

    .otodor-pop__close {
      position: absolute; top: 0.85rem; right: 0.85rem; z-index: 2;
      width: 32px; height: 32px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      padding: 0; border: none; border-radius: 50%; cursor: pointer;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.07); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);
      transition: background 160ms ease, color 160ms ease;
    }
    .otodor-pop__close svg { width: 13px; height: 13px; display: block; pointer-events: none; }
    .otodor-pop__close:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.16); color: #fff; }
    .otodor-pop :focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--otodor-blue, #4DA6FF); outline-offset: 2px; }

    @keyframes otodor-pop-fade { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }
    @keyframes otodor-pop-rise { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px) scale(0.99); } to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .otodor-pop__backdrop, .otodor-pop__dialog { animation: none; }
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}

  <div
    class="otodor-pop"
    data-otodor-popup
    data-popup-key="{{ popup_key | escape }}"
    data-delay="{{ section.settings.delay | default: 6 }}"
    data-scroll="{{ section.settings.scroll_trigger | default: 0 }}"
    data-remember-days="{{ section.settings.remember_days | default: 7 }}"
    data-open="false"
    hidden
  >
    <div class="otodor-pop__backdrop" data-otodor-popup-close></div>

    <div
      class="otodor-pop__dialog"
      role="dialog"
      aria-modal="true"
      aria-labelledby="otodor-pop-title-{{ section.id }}"
    >
      <button type="button" class="otodor-pop__close" data-otodor-popup-close aria-label="Close">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M1.5 1.5 12.5 12.5M12.5 1.5 1.5 12.5" />
        </svg>
      </button>

      {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
        <div class="otodor-pop__media">
          {{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 700 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', alt: '', widths: '350, 700' }}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="otodor-pop__body">
        {%- assign eyebrow = section.settings.eyebrow | default: settings.otodor_campaign_name -%}
        {%- if eyebrow != blank -%}
          <span class="otodor-pop__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow | escape }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}

        <h2 class="otodor-pop__title" id="otodor-pop-title-{{ section.id }}">
          {{ section.settings.heading | escape }}
        </h2>

        {%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}
          <p class="otodor-pop__text">{{ section.settings.text | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="otodor-pop__coupon">
          <span class="otodor-pop__code">{{ coupon_code | escape }}</span>
          {%- comment -%}
            Text-only on purpose: otodor-offer.js swaps this button's
            textContent for the "copied" label, so any markup inside would be
            thrown away on the first click.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button type="button" class="otodor-pop__copy"
            data-otodor-copy="{{ coupon_code | escape }}"
            data-copied-label="{{ section.settings.copied_label | default: 'Copied' | escape }}">{{ section.settings.copy_label | default: 'Copy' | escape }}</button>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          The offer's value is generated, not typed — change the coupon in theme
          settings and this line follows, with no stale number left in the copy.
          It sits under the code as a caption, the way a store states what a
          voucher is worth and where it applies.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if coupon_amount > 0 -%}
          <p class="otodor-pop__value">
            <strong>₹{% render 'otodor-rupees', amount: coupon_amount %} off</strong>{% if settings.otodor_coupon_scope_label != blank %} · {{ settings.otodor_coupon_scope_label | escape }}{% endif %}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if settings.otodor_free_delivery or settings.otodor_emi_enabled -%}
          <ul class="otodor-pop__perks" role="list">
            {%- if settings.otodor_free_delivery and settings.otodor_free_delivery_label != blank -%}
              <li class="otodor-pop__perk">
                <span aria-hidden="true">{% render 'otodor-icon', name: 'installation' %}</span>
                {{ settings.otodor_free_delivery_label | escape }}
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if settings.otodor_emi_enabled -%}
              <li class="otodor-pop__perk">
                <span aria-hidden="true">{% render 'otodor-icon', name: 'log' %}</span>
                {{ section.settings.emi_label | default: 'EMI options available' | escape }}
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="otodor-pop__actions">
          {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
            <a class="otodor-pop__cta" href="{{ section.settings.cta_link | default: '/collections/all' }}" data-otodor-popup-cta>
              {{ section.settings.cta_label | escape }}
              <span aria-hidden="true">{% render 'otodor-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}</span>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.dismiss_label != blank -%}
            <button type="button" class="otodor-pop__later" data-otodor-popup-close>{{ section.settings.dismiss_label | escape }}</button>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if section.settings.fine_print != blank -%}
          <p class="otodor-pop__fine">{{ section.settings.fine_print | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "OTODOR Offer Popup",
  "tag": "div",
  "class": "otodor-popup-mount",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The campaign popup. It reads the coupon, delivery and EMI wording from Theme settings → OTODOR Offers, Pricing & EMI, and hides itself outside the campaign dates — so ending a sale is a date, not an edit." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enabled", "label": "Enabled", "default": true },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Copy" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "info": "Blank = the campaign name from theme settings." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Sale pricing, unlocked.", "info": "The coupon value and scope are printed for you from theme settings — no number to keep in step here." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Text", "default": "Independence Day pricing on the OTODOR wooden-door range. Apply the code at checkout and the ZEAL lands at ₹6,200 including GST." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "code_override", "label": "Discount code override", "info": "Blank = the code from theme settings." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "copy_label", "label": "Copy button label", "default": "Copy" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "copied_label", "label": "Copied confirmation", "default": "Copied" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "emi_label", "label": "EMI line", "default": "EMI options available" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Shop wooden door locks" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_link", "label": "Button link" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "dismiss_label", "label": "Dismiss link label", "default": "No thanks" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "fine_print", "label": "Fine print", "default": "Valid on Wooden Door Locks only, while the sale runs. One code per order." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image", "info": "Optional. Hidden on phones." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Where it shows" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "target", "label": "Pages", "default": "shopping",
      "options": [
        { "value": "all", "label": "Every page" },
        { "value": "home", "label": "Homepage only" },
        { "value": "shopping", "label": "Homepage, collections & products" },
        { "value": "scoped", "label": "Only where the coupon applies" }
      ]
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "When it shows" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "delay", "label": "Delay before showing", "min": 0, "max": 30, "step": 1, "unit": "s", "default": 6 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "scroll_trigger", "label": "…or once scrolled past", "min": 0, "max": 90, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 0, "info": "0 = time only. Otherwise whichever happens first." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "remember_days", "label": "Don't show again for", "min": 1, "max": 90, "step": 1, "unit": "d", "default": 7, "info": "Copying the code suppresses it for a year." }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
